abstract: >-
  This technical research note examines the compositional privacy risk of AI text watermarking and model provenance. It introduces provenance-mediated identity linkage: the risk that a non-identifying model-level provenance signal may still contribute to generation-event, account, organization, or human attribution when correlated with retained generation records, timestamps, session data, account metadata, semantic fingerprints, platform records, or other auxiliary information. It proposes a Compositional Privacy Invariant requiring identity-resolution transitions to be treated as separately authorized disclosure events.
